# Minception — Windsurf Rules

## Project
Minception — API Mock Gateway
Monorepo: mock-service (FastAPI :8001) + admin-service (FastAPI :8002) + frontend (React :3000)
Database: MongoDB Atlas with embedded document model

## Core Principle
This is a **mock API platform**. The core data model is:
`Gateway` → embedded `Endpoints[]` → embedded `Flavors[]`
One MongoDB query returns everything needed to serve a mock response.

## Python/FastAPI
- Python 3.11+ with full type hints
- Pydantic v2 models — always use response_model on routes
- motor (AsyncIOMotorClient) for all DB operations — never synchronous
- All handlers: `async def`
- Routes use APIRouter with prefix/tags
- Auth: `Depends(require_role(["admin"]))` pattern
- Errors: raise HTTPException(status, detail={"code": "...", "message": "..."})
- Response shape: `{"success": bool, "data": ..., "error": null | {"code", "message"}}`

## TypeScript/React
- React 18 + TypeScript strict mode
- React Query (TanStack v5) for server state
- Axios in src/services/api.ts with JWT interceptor
- Tailwind + Shadcn/ui components
- No Redux — auth state via AuthContext only

## MongoDB
- Embedded: gateways.endpoints[].flavors[] — do NOT split into separate collections
- Always ObjectId for _id
- Timestamps: created_at, updated_at
- Use $push/$pull/$set for nested document operations

## File Structure
```
mock-service/app/engine.py     ← flavor matching engine (most critical)
mock-service/app/mongo.py      ← motor connection
admin-service/app/auth/        ← JWT + bcrypt + role dependencies
admin-service/app/routes/      ← CRUD route handlers
migrations/versions/           ← sequential migration files 001_xxx.py
```

## Don'ts
- No Redis
- No raw pymongo in route handlers
- No `any` in TypeScript
- No secrets in source code — env vars only
- Don't normalize the embedded document model
- Don't push to main/develop directly
